WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:03.340
Going into Terminator: Dark Fate, you might
have some questions…

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.670
"So you're Carl?"

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.330
"That's what everybody calls me, yes."

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:11.560
Not to worry: We've prepared a crash course
in all things Terminator, giving you a rundown

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:15.770
on past films and letting you know just what
to expect from the latest installment.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:18.020
"Come with me if you want to live."

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.020
The Terminator

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.820
First, let's talk about what's gone down so
far, starting with The Terminator, the film

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.220
that got the ball rolling.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:29.390
In 1984, a young waitress named Sarah Connor
is targeted by a hulking cyborg and rescued

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:33.870
by a young buck named Kyle, who explains that
both he and her would-be assassin are from

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:35.609
the year 2029.

00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:39.329
He goes on to demonstrate that he can drive
and rattle off pages of exposition at the

00:00:39.329 --> 00:00:40.329
same time:

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:44.300
"All right, listen, The Terminator's an infiltration
unit.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.620
Part man, part machine.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.010
Underneath, it's a hyperalloy combat chassis."

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:54.370
Kyle goes on to reveal that in this far-flung
future, Sarah's unborn son John is a warlord

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:59.879
in the fight against an army of killer robots,
known somewhat artlessly as the Machines.

00:00:59.879 --> 00:01:03.999
He further explains that he has been sent
to protect Sarah, while the robotic beefcake

00:01:03.999 --> 00:01:05.610
has been sent to kill her.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:10.030
Over the course of the film, Sarah learns
that humanity is heading towards nuclear annihilation

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:11.100
in the near future.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.970
In fact, her son John will be the last great
hope of the human race.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:20.220
By the end of The Terminator, Kyle has impregnated
Sarah after a steamy motel interlude… and

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.110
he eventually sacrifices himself in the hopes
of destroying the Terminator.

00:01:24.110 --> 00:01:28.540
It's ultimately Sarah who kills the offending
machine with the help of a pneumatic press.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.680
And with that, Sarah drives off into the horizon.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.350
Terminator 2: Judgment Day

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.870
Then we arrive at Terminator 2: Judgment Day.

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:50.010
Released in 1991 but set in 1995, T2 sees
Sarah locked up in a psych ward… because

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.490
she can't stop talking about robots coming
from the future to tear our lives asunder.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.740
She's also prone to acting out.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.000
(When someone says they actually liked Terminator 3.)

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.390
Her son John bounces between foster homes
until one day, a guy in a leather jacket saves

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.380
him from a police officer who can morph into
liquid metal.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:13.379
It turns out Leather Jacket Guy is a reprogrammed
Terminator sent back in time by Future John.

00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:14.459
The mission?

00:02:14.459 --> 00:02:20.060
To save Present John from another robot...
who himself was sent back in time to kill

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:21.299
Present John.

00:02:21.299 --> 00:02:22.430
Isn't time travel fun?

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:25.299
Together, John and the Terminator rescue Sarah.

00:02:25.299 --> 00:02:28.060
"Come with me if you want to live."

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.900
The three of them ultimately destroy the gloopy
metal Bad Guy with a combination of liquid

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:33.840
nitrogen and molten steel.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:38.170
Shortly thereafter, the Good Guy Terminator
descends into a vat of molten metal.

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.939
Hooray, the world is saved!

00:02:39.939 --> 00:02:41.310
Or is it?

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.549
Forget those other sequels

00:02:42.549 --> 00:02:46.810
The minds behind Terminator: Dark Fate have
decided to ignore several installments of

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:47.930
the franchise (so did we).

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.779
In interviews, director Tim Miller has said
the film will serve as a direct sequel to

00:02:51.779 --> 00:02:55.689
The Terminator and Terminator 2: Judgment
Day … so let's take a quick look at what

00:02:55.689 --> 00:02:56.920
we're ditching here.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.240
"Do you wanna live?

00:02:58.240 --> 00:02:59.100
Come on!"

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:05.080
Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines is out
of the picture and frankly, that's okay.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:07.880
"Talk to the hand…."

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:17.550
It also means Judgment Day still hasn't taken
place in the upcoming film.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.549
"The Terminator knew…

00:03:19.549 --> 00:03:21.439
He tried to tell us.

00:03:21.439 --> 00:03:25.349
But I didn't want to hear it."

00:03:25.349 --> 00:03:28.430
Terminator: Salvation doesn't concern us anymore.

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.120
"Come with me if you want to live."

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:34.639
Feel free to wipe it from your memory bank...
if you haven't already.

00:03:34.639 --> 00:03:38.400
And while you're at it, we're expected to
act like Terminator Genisys never happened

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.359
either… and frankly, we can live with that.

00:03:41.359 --> 00:03:43.480
"I won't allow this."

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.389
"Whaddya gonna do - talk us to death?

00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:49.450
You don't even have a body."

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:52.319
Oh, and remember the TV show The Sarah Connor
Chronicles?

00:03:52.319 --> 00:03:56.029
Well, go ahead and forget that, too... at
least when it comes to the new film.

00:03:56.029 --> 00:03:57.439
What's the story?

00:03:57.439 --> 00:04:03.049
Terminator: Dark Fate is set a full 27 years
after Terminator 2 and it introduces us to

00:04:03.049 --> 00:04:08.019
a dangerous new Terminator model called Rev-9,
portrayed by Gabriel Luna.

00:04:08.019 --> 00:04:12.489
"He's the most lethal Terminator ever created."

00:04:12.489 --> 00:04:17.110
And here's Grace, a super-soldier from the
future portrayed by Mackenzie Davis.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.790
"I am human.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:20.790
Just enhanced."

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:25.530
Grace has been sent back in time to protect
Dani Ramos, played by Natalia Reyes.

00:04:25.530 --> 00:04:28.030
She's a young woman who's being relentlessly
hunted by Rev-9.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.690
"That is not your father.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.130
Come with me or you're dead in the next thirty
seconds."

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:38.460
Soon, a certain fierce warrior named Sarah
Connor and your favorite T-800 enter the fray,

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:40.960
doing everything in their power to save Dani
from Rev-9.

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.970
Naturally, the fate of the whole world is
in their hands.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:48.560
"If you don't make it, everybody dies."

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:50.420
Rated R

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:54.590
One thing Terminator: Dark Fate shares with
the first two James Cameron movies: it's rated

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:59.280
R … and that hasn't been the case for a
Terminator film in over 15 years.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.280
As Cameron says,

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:05.640
"It's R-rated, it's grim, it's gritty, it's
fast, it's intense."

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:10.480
In 2009, Terminator Salvation became the first
film in the franchise to receive a PG-13 rating,

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.760
with Terminator Genisys following suit in
2015.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:21.350
"I know now why you cry, but it's something
I can never do."

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:24.490
At least one cast member is thrilled about
the R-rating.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:27.030
In a Reddit AMA, Arnold Schwarzenegger revealed:

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:31.680
"I was sick and tired with the last time,
when the studio decided to make it a PG-13

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.090
rating just because they thought there [were]
more dollars in there.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:37.900
I said, ‘Guys you’re so stupid…this
is [...] not Terminator the babysitter type

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:38.900
of thing.'"

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.250
No, it's not… but wasn't that the plot to
Kindergarten Cop?

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:45.790
"First, I would just like to get to know you."

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:46.790
(laughing)

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.760
The T-800 is back

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:53.390
This is Arnold Schwarzenegger's fifth appearance
as an "800 series" Terminator or the sixth

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.580
if you count the CGI Arnold in Terminator:
Salvation.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:06.760
But Schwarzenegger's character in Terminator:
Dark Fate is apparently not the same machine

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:11.080
we came to fear in The Terminator … nor
is he the hunk of metal we came to love in

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.080
T2.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:17.140
Director Tim Miller confirmed in an interview
that this is an all-new machine, telling ComicBook.com:

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:21.790
"Imagine the rules that [original director
James Cameron] set down, about what would

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:25.760
happen with a Terminator, what they become,
they're a learning machine, they're a neural

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.480
net, they just keep learning.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:32.230
So the longer you leave one around in our
society, the more he learns about humanity.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:33.680
And then what does he become?"

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.820
We have no idea.

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:37.510
But Miller clearly isn't afraid to ask the
tough questions.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:39.190
James Cameron's return

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:44.130
James Cameron is arguably the only guy who
ever got a Terminator movie just right…

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:47.440
but he hasn't been involved in a Terminator
film since 1991.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.420
Well, that changes with Terminator: Dark Fate.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:51.450
As Deadline reports:

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:54.810
"Cameron wrote the story treatment and took
a hands-on producer role."

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:59.040
And if audiences respond positively to the
new film, it sounds like there could be more

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.510
entries on the way.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:01.510
Cameron told Deadline:

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:06.220
"[We're looking] at it as a three-film arc,
so there is a greater story there to be told.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:10.050
If we get fortunate enough to make some money
with Dark Fate we know exactly where we can

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:11.860
go with the subsequent films."

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:13.030
Here's hoping.

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:19.300
"I'll be back."

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:21.560
